solution_md:
Coord bash FTW

   Let A $(x_a,\frac{1}{x_a})$ ,B $(x_b,\frac{1}{x_b})$  and  P $(x_p,\frac{1}{x_p})$  such that  $x_a,x_b>0$  and  $x_a>x_b$ . Hence we can say that 
    \begin{align*}
       2\Delta = \det\begin{vmatrix}
        1 & x_a & \frac{1}{x_a} 
        1 & x_b & \frac{1}{x_b}
        1 & x_p & \frac{1}{x_p}
   \end{vmatrix} = \det\begin{vmatrix}
    0 & x_a-x_b  & \frac{1}{x_a}-\frac{1}{x_b} 
    0 & x_b-x_p & \frac{1}{x_b}-\frac{1}{x_p}
    1 & x_p & \frac{1}{x_p}
\end{vmatrix}
2\Delta= \left|(x_a-x_b)\left(\frac{1}{x_b}-\frac{1}{x_p}\right)-(x_b-x_p)\left(\frac{1}{x_a}-\frac{1}{x_b}\right)\right|
2\Delta=\left|\frac{x_a}{x_b}-\frac{x_b}{x_a}+\frac{x_b-x_a}{x_p}+x_p\frac{x_b-x_a}{x_bx_a}\right|
2\Delta=\left|\frac{x_a}{x_b}-\frac{x_b}{x_a}-(x_a-x_b)\left(\frac{1}{x_p}+\frac{x_p}{x_ax_b}\right)\right|
    \end{align*}
For  $\Delta$  to be maximum  $\frac{1}{x_p}+\frac{x_p}{x_ax_b}$  should be minimum.

<span style="color:#00f">Claim: Let  $E=\frac{1}{m}+\frac{m}{c}$  then  $\min\{E\}$  exist at  $m=\sqrt{c}$ </span>**Proof:**
Second order derivative method.  $\blacksquare$ Hence we have  $x_p=\sqrt{x_ax_b}$ . We will calculate the area bounded by the chords.

1) Area between  $BP$  and hyperbola. 
\begin{align*}
    \Delta_{BP}=\frac{(\sqrt{x_bx_a}-x_b)(\frac{1}{\sqrt{x_ax_b}}+\frac{1}{x_b})}{2}-\ln\left(\frac{\sqrt{x_ax_b}}{x_b}\right)=\frac{(\sqrt{x_a}-\sqrt{x_b})(\frac{1}{\sqrt{x_a}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{x_b}})}{2}-\ln\left(\sqrt{\frac{x_a}{x_b}}\right)
\end{align*}
2) Area between  $AP$  and hyperbola. 
\begin{align*}
    \Delta_{AP}=\frac{(x_a-\sqrt{x_bx_a})(\frac{1}{\sqrt{x_ax_b}}+\frac{1}{x_a})}{2}-\ln\left(\frac{x_a}{\sqrt{x_ax_b}}\right)=\frac{(\sqrt{x_a}-\sqrt{x_b})(\frac{1}{\sqrt{x_a}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{x_b}})}{2}-\ln\left(\sqrt{\frac{x_a}{x_b}}\right)
\end{align*} $\blacksquare$

