\[\{a_1,a_2,\dots\}<\{a_1+\varepsilon,a_2-2\varepsilon,\dots\}<\{a_1-\varepsilon,a_2-\varepsilon,\dots\},\]
contradiction.

Now let  $k$  be the value such that  $B_k$  is greater than  $A$ . Then we claim that the rule is simply comparing  $a_k$  and  $b_k$ . To do this, we will prove that if  $a_k<b_k$ , then  $A<B$ .

