However noting that  $Q$  satisfies  $-1 = (MD,PQ)$ , we must have  $\overline{PK} \cap \Gamma = Q$ . Then  $Q$  lies on  $\overline{PK}$ , or equivalently  $\overline{PS}$ .  $\blacksquare$

