Now computing coordinates we have  $a = 0$ ,  $T_1 = t$  and  $T_2 = \frac{1}{t}$ . Also  $m = \frac{t^2 + 1}{2t}$ . Clearly  $B$  is the reflection of  $A$  over  $M$  so  $b = \frac{t^2+1}{t}$ . Now note that it follows form simple angle chasing that  $X_1X_2$  is a diameter of  $\omega$  so it suffices to show  $T_1X_1 \perp T_2X_2$ . Note that  $x_1 = 1$  and  $x_2$  =  $\frac{t^2+1}{t} + 1$ . Now it suffices to show,
\begin{align*}
    \frac{t - 1}{\frac{1}{t} - \frac{t^2+t+1}{t}} &= - \overline{\left( \frac{t - 1}{\frac{1}{t} - \frac{t^2+t+1}{t}} \right)}
    &= -\overline{\left(\frac{t^2 - t}{-t^2 - t} \right)}
    &= \frac{1 - t}{1+t}
