A quick computation shows that  $M$  is the midpoint of  $\overline{X^*Y^*}$ . Moreover,  $S$  and  $T$  are sent to points  $S^*,T^*$  on the circumcircle, implying  $\overline{AS^*}$  and  $\overline{AT^*}$  isogonal. So  $\overline{AS}$  and  $\overline{AT}$  are isogonal, implying  $K$  is on  $(AST)$ . Then the homothety sending  $(AST)$  to  $(ABC)$  sends  $K$  to  $M$ , which implies the desired.

