Note that 
\begin{align*}\tan \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\tan \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\tan \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right) &= \frac{\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}{\cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\cos \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}  &= \frac{8\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)^2\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}{8\sin \left(\frac{\pi }{7}  \right)\cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\cos \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}  &= \frac{8\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)^2\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}{4 \sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi }{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}  &= \frac{8\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)^2\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}{-2 \sin \left(\frac{4\pi}{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{4 \pi }{7} \right)}  &= \frac{8\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)^2\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}{-\sin \left(\frac{8 \pi }{7} \right)}  &= \frac{8\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)^2\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right)}{\sin \left(\frac{\pi }{7} \right)}  &= 8 \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right) \end{align*}
From this, we also see that  $\cos \left( \frac{\pi}{7}\right) \cos \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{4\pi}{7} \right) = \frac{1}{8}$ .  Note that
\begin{align*}8\sin^2 \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\sin^2 \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin^2 \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right) &= \left(1 - \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right) \right)\left(1 - \cos \left(\frac{4 \pi}{7} \right) \right)\left(1 - \cos \left(\frac{6 \pi}{7} \right) \right)  &=  \left(1 - \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right) \right)\left(1 + \cos \left(\frac{3 \pi}{7} \right) \right)\left(1 + \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right) \right)  &= 1 + \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7}\right) - \cos \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right) + \cos \left(\frac{3\pi}{7}\right)  &- \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right)\cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{7} \right) - \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right) + \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi }{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)  &-\cos \left( \frac{\pi}{7}\right)\cos \left( \frac{2\pi}{7}\right)\cos \left( \frac{3\pi}{7}\right) \end{align*}
Notice that since  $\cos a \cos b = \frac{1}{2} \left(\cos (a-b) + \cos(a+b) \right)$ . thus, we can write:
\begin{align*}- \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right)\cos\left(\frac{3 \pi}{7} \right) - \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right) + \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi }{7} \right) \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)= \end{align*} \begin{align*}\frac{1}{2} \left(-\cos \left(\frac{5 \pi}{7} \right) - \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{7} \right) - \cos \left(\frac{3 \pi}{7} \right) - \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right) + \cos \left(\frac{4 \pi}{7} \right) + \cos \left(\frac{2 \pi}{7} \right) \right) =\end{align*} \begin{align*} -\cos \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right) + \cos \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right) - \cos \left( \frac{3\pi}{7} \right) \end{align*}
Therefore,
\begin{align*}8\sin^2 \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\sin^2 \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin^2 \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right) = \frac{7}{8} \Longleftrightarrow \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{2\pi}{7} \right)\sin \left(\frac{3\pi}{7} \right) = \frac{\sqrt{7}}{8} \end{align*}
from which we get a final answer of  $\boxed{\sqrt{7}}$ .

